The board of commissioners of the county shall annually review and, as deemed necessary by the commission, update the identity theft prevention program along with any relevant red flags in order to reflect changes in risks to customers or to the safety and soundness of the city and its covered accounts from identity theft. In so doing, the board of commissioners shall consider the following factors and exercise its discretion in amending the program:
(1) The county's experiences with identity theft;
(2) Updates in methods of identity theft;
(3) Updates in customary methods used to detect, prevent, and mitigate identity theft;
